User Story: Customer Login for Ecommerce Application
Title: Login to Ecommerce Account

As a registered ecommerce customer,
I want to securely log in to my account using my email address or mobile number and password,
So that I can access my personal account, view order history, manage my cart and wishlist, update shipping details, and complete purchases faster.

Description
The ecommerce application should provide a secure and user-friendly login functionality for registered customers. Users should be able to enter valid credentials, receive appropriate validation messages, and access their account after successful authentication.

Acceptance Criteria
Login Page Access

Given the user is on the ecommerce website or app,
When the user clicks the Login or Sign In option,
Then the system should display the login page/form.
Valid Login

Given the user has a registered account,
When the user enters a valid email/mobile number and password,
And clicks the Login button,
Then the system should authenticate the user,
And redirect the user to the homepage, account dashboard, or previously visited checkout/cart page.
Invalid Credentials

Given the user enters an incorrect email/mobile number or password,
When the user clicks the Login button,
Then the system should display an error message such as:
“Invalid email/mobile number or password.”
Required Field Validation

Given the user leaves the email/mobile number or password field empty,
When the user clicks the Login button,
Then the system should display validation messages:
Email/mobile number is required
Password is required
Password Masking

Given the user enters a password,
Then the password should be hidden/masked by default.
The user may have an option to show or hide the password.
Forgot Password

Given the user has forgotten their password,
When the user clicks Forgot Password,
Then the system should navigate the user to the password recovery flow.
Remember Me

Given the user selects Remember Me,
When login is successful,
Then the system may keep the user signed in for future visits based on security policy.
Account Lock/Security

Given the user enters incorrect credentials multiple times,
When the allowed number of attempts is exceeded,
Then the system should temporarily block login attempts or show additional verification.
Successful Session

Given the login is successful,
Then the system should create a secure user session,
And display the user as logged in across the application.
Business Rules
Only registered users should be able to log in.
Passwords must be securely stored and never displayed in plain text.
Login should use secure communication such as HTTPS.
Error messages should not reveal whether the email/mobile number or password is incorrect.
Users should be redirected back to checkout if they were trying to purchase before login.
Priority
High

Dependencies
User registration functionality
Authentication service/API
Password recovery functionality
User account/dashboard module